  "term": "unilateral lesion",
  "definition": "A unilateral lesion is damage or disruption affecting one side of a paired body or brain system. In the source, it refers to one-sided injury in vestibular or dopaminergic pathways and is discussed in terms of the movement changes that can follow when only one side is impaired.",
